Printing Demos and Utility Directory

The Classes defined in these files are:
	
Category System-Printing
	Document
	FontDescription
	FontStyle
	PageStyle
	PostscriptPrinter

These files implement translators that can turn Smalltalk text and Forms into PostScript programs suitable for printing.

The proper order to file these sources in is:
	Printing.st
	PrtSuprt.st
	TextMenu.st
	PrtOutOS.st

Reading in the file Printing.st will initialize the printing classes and read
in the Adobe font metric files held in the AFM subdirectory.  The
initialization method in class FontDescription will prompt you for the
directory name in which to look for the font metric files.  These are found
in the 'AFM' subdirectory of the 'printing' directory in the standard release.

